nd":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The theme, submission process, participant roles, venue, and audience arrangements change by edition; follow current (Pause.) notices.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"lewis-clark-international-affairs-symposium","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"International Affairs Symposium","title":"Stage Global Disagreements as Live Debate","subtitle":"Students organize opposing viewpoints on international dilemmas","notes":"Choose a debate, keynote, screening, or discussion from the annual program, then read the session description so you understand the competing positions.","short_summary":"Student organizers bring policy experts and public figures into structured debates about contested international questions.","evidence_claim":"Lewis & Clark identifies the International Affairs Symposium as an annual student-organized symposium begun in 1966, built around debates featuring experts and public figures with opposing viewpoints.","source_url":"https://college.lclark.edu/academics/symposia/our-symposia/","source_title":"Our Symposia","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Themes, speakers, locations, and attendance arrangements change annually; consult the symposium’s current program.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"lewis-clark-race-monologues","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Race Monologues","title":"Listen Without Interrupting the Monologues","subtitle":"Student-authored narratives close the Ray Warren Symposium tradition","notes":"Attend prepared to listen respectfully, hold applause or audible reactions until the final monologue ends, and let each presenter choose whether to talk afterward.","short_summary":"Students share self-authored reflections on racial and ethnic identity through prose, poetry, song, and collaborative writing.","evidence_claim":"Lewis & Clark states that students began Race Monologues in 2002 and that the original narratives have been presented annually at the Ray Warren Symposium since 2004.","source_url":"https://college.lclark.edu/programs/ethnic_studies/symposium/race-monologues/","source_title":"Race Monologues","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The official guidance welcomes respectful listeners and asks audiences to withhold applause and audible responses until the final monologue concludes.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
